  "configuration_id": "config_001",
  "reason": "With no prior evidence, the most informative first step is to establish the simplest RNA-only baseline (singleprofile, PCA-2000). This gives a performance floor for the RNA modality with minimal complexity, which is essential before exploring learned encoders (scvi, scgpt), multiprofile aggregation, image modality, or multimodal fusion. Knowing the RNA baseline accuracy lets me calibrate whether more complex designs (multiprofile, scgpt, multimodal) actually improve over a simple linear-projection model, and it anchors all subsequent comparisons. It is the lowest-risk, highest-information experiment to open the search under a tight 10-run budget."
}

